It should convert double quotes to single quotes in Twig function calls (base case)
{{ stimulus_controller("controller-name") }}
<div class="class name"></div>

It should keep double quotes if the string contains single quotes
{{ stimulus_controller("it's a name") }}

It should convert double quotes to single quotes in tag base case
{% set foo = "bar" %}

It should handle multiple arguments with quotes
{{ some_function("arg1", "arg2") }}

It should convert to double quotes when twigSingleQuote is false
twigSingleQuote: false
{{ stimulus_controller('controller-name') }}

It should keep single quotes if string contains double quotes when twigSingleQuote is false
twigSingleQuote: false
{{ stimulus_controller('say "hello"') }}

It should not modify HTML attributes within Twig comments
{# <div class="should-not-change"></div> #}

It should not convert quotes nested inside a string of the preferred style
{% set a = 'say "hi"' %}

It should not convert nested quotes in ternary expressions
{{ x ? 'a="b"' }}

It should not convert strings containing escapes
{% set a = "say \"hi\"" %}

It should still convert convertible strings next to nested-quote strings
{{ foo("plain", 'say "hi"') }}

It should not convert quotes nested inside a double-quoted string when twigSingleQuote is false
twigSingleQuote: false
{% set a = "say 'hi'" %}

It should not convert double-quoted strings containing interpolation
{% set key = "#{opt.name}:#{opt.value}" %}

It should not convert single-quoted strings containing interpolation when twigSingleQuote is false
twigSingleQuote: false
{% set key = '#{literal}' %}

It should still convert strings with a bare hash
{% set a = "plain #tag" %}

It should not convert a double-quoted interpolated string
{{ "#{x}" }}

It should not convert a single-quoted literal hash brace when twigSingleQuote is false
twigSingleQuote: false
{{ '#{x}' }}

It should not convert interpolated strings in conditions
{% if a == "#{x}" %}
  yes
{% elseif b == "#{y}" %}
  no
{% endif %}

It should not convert single-quoted literal hash braces in conditions when twigSingleQuote is false
twigSingleQuote: false
{% if a == '#{x}' %}yes{% endif %}

It should not convert an interpolated include template
{% include "#{x}.twig" %}

It should not convert a single-quoted include template when twigSingleQuote is false
twigSingleQuote: false
{% include '#{x}.twig' %}

It should not convert interpolated strings in lookups
{{ a["#{x}"] }}

It should not convert single-quoted literal hash braces in lookups when twigSingleQuote is false
twigSingleQuote: false
{{ a['#{x}'] }}

It should still convert other strings in lookups
{{ a["x y"] }}

It should not convert interpolated strings in filter arguments
{{ a | f: "#{x}", "y" }}

It should not convert interpolated strings in attributes
<a href="{{ "#{x}" }}"></a>

It should not convert double-quoted strings containing a backslash
{{ "a\n" }}
{{ "\#{x}" }}

It should not convert single-quoted strings containing a backslash when twigSingleQuote is false
twigSingleQuote: false
{{ 'a\n' }}

It should not convert quotes nested inside of interpolation
{{ "#{a["b"]}" }}

It should still convert convertible strings next to nested interpolation
{{ "#{f({k: "v"})} x" ~ "y" }}

It should not treat a hash brace in a single-quoted string as interpolation
{{ '#{x' ~ "y" }}
